WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.530
I need you to imagine this: it's 2:07 a.m., my laptop

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.140
is balanced on a laundry basket, and I'm eating

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.700
cereal out of a coffee mug…

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.480
because I'm an entrepreneur now.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.700
I had just launched my first "real"

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.850
business: a tiny online shop selling custom productivity

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.910
planners for freelancers.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.920
Nothing fancy—just clean designs, funny prompts,

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.920
and the occasional passive-aggressive sticker like

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:29.120
"Did you actually send that invoice?"

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.670
I refresh my store dashboard one more time, expecting

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.890
the usual: one order, maybe two if my mom gets excited.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.640
Then my screen updates.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.990
And I see it.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:43.870
A single order.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.950
For 500 planners.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:54.770
Total: $12,480. I just stare at it like it's going

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.520
to apologize and turn into a typo.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:03.560
"Five… hundred?" My heart starts doing parkour in

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.420
my chest. I'm not a business owner.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.330
I'm a person with Wi‑Fi and a dream.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.270
I click into the details, already mentally spending

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.080
the profit on adult things like…

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.890
a chair with lumbar support.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.570
The customer name is "Elliot Graye."

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.590
The email looks legit.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.260
The payment cleared.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.090
And then I see the shipping address.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:30.440
It's an industrial street on the edge of town.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.230
No suite number.

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:33.690
No business name.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.530
Just a street address.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:38.670
I zoom in on the map.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.960
It's… an abandoned warehouse.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.790
Not "cool startup loft"

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.690
warehouse. Like, "a raccoon probably pays rent here"

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.880
warehouse. I feel the excitement drain out of me

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.530
like someone pulled the plug.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:59.550
Because there are only two possibilities: One: a

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.940
mysterious billionaire loves planners.

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:07.230
Two: I am about to get spectacularly scammed.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:12.700
Okay. Three possibilities: maybe the raccoon is

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:15.880
the billionaire. I email the customer.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.900
"Hey Elliot! Huge thanks for your order—just confirming

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.990
delivery details for such a large shipment."

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.770
Five minutes later, a reply pops in.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:30.190
"Ship ASAP. Need by Friday.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.610
Don't call. Busy."

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:37.010
And then, like a cherry on top of the stress sundae:

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.340
"Also send tracking immediately."

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:44.520
My brain starts listing every horror story I've

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.700
ever read: chargebacks, fake cards, "delivered"

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.850
disputes, the classic "I never received it"

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:55.350
performance. I walk to my living room, which is

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:58.240
also my office, which is also my dining room.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.600
And I do the thing every entrepreneur does when

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.920
faced with danger: I call my friend Maya.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.690
Maya picks up on the second ring.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.830
"If this is about your plants again, I told you:

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.610
talking to them doesn't count as marketing."

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:17.050
"Maya. I got a twelve-thousand-dollar order.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.730
And it's going to an abandoned warehouse."

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:21.580
There's a beat.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:25.020
"Okay. Do not ship that."

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.080
"But what if it's real?"

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.320
"Then they can confirm the address like a normal

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.370
human and not like a movie villain."

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.920
I hang up and sit back down, trying to breathe like

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.310
a calm person who definitely doesn't own three "How

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:40.870
to Start a Business"

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.550
books and zero common sense.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.590
I decide to do a little digging.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.400
First: I Google the address.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.070
Nothing. Second: I search the name "Elliot Graye."

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.810
I get an actor.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:59.230
A dentist. A guy selling used jet skis.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.090
Third: I search the email.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:03.990
It's linked to…

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:07.720
nothing. My stomach drops.

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:12.435
This is the part where horror movies say, "Don't

00:04:12.435 --> 00:04:13.684
open the door."

00:04:13.684 --> 00:04:15.310
Then I get another email.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.680
"Why no tracking yet?"

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.050
It's been fourteen minutes since the order.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.560
I reply, keeping it polite.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.220
"Hi! For high-volume orders, we confirm shipping

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.440
details for security.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:31.200
Could you tell me the business name at the delivery

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.710
location and a contact number?"

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:36.150
The response arrives instantly.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.040
"No time. Ship now.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.180
I paid." Now my hands are cold.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.350
That's not a customer.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.270
That's a countdown.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:52.330
I stand up, pace in a tiny circle, and then I do

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.230
something I've never done in my life.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:58.040
I call the number on the payment processor.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.560
After being serenaded by hold music that sounds

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:04.440
like a depressed elevator, a rep answers.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:09.870
"Hi—sorry—this might sound weird, but can you tell

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.430
me if this payment looks risky?

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:14.510
Big order, sketchy address."

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.620
The rep goes quiet.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:20.920
"I can't confirm details…

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:25.300
but I can tell you this: the transaction is marked

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:29.360
'high risk.'" My face goes hot.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:34.960
"So… scam." "It could be fraud, yes."

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.470
I thank them, hang up, and stare at my screen like

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:40.080
it betrayed me personally.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.570
Then another email hits.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:47.820
"If you don't ship in 1 hour I will report you.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.720
Refund me now."

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:51.550
I blink. Wait.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:54.970
They want a refund now?

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:58.670
That's when it clicks—like a puzzle piece snapping

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.870
into place. This isn't about planners.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.740
It's about pressure.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.320
They want me to panic and hit "refund,"

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.080
and maybe they've already set up some trick where

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.900
the money goes somewhere else.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:15.200
Or they want proof of shipment so they can win a

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:19.380
dispute. Either way, I'm not becoming a cautionary

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:20.420
tale on the internet.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:22.180
I type back.

00:06:23.429 --> 00:06:24.539
"Thanks for your message.

00:06:24.539 --> 00:06:28.389
Due to security policy, we require address verification

00:06:28.399 --> 00:06:29.709
for high-value orders.

00:06:30.529 --> 00:06:32.989
If you prefer, I can cancel and the payment will

00:06:32.999 --> 00:06:35.539
be voided." Not refunded.

00:06:35.539 --> 00:06:38.789
Voided. Two minutes pass.

00:06:39.749 --> 00:06:41.419
Then I get a reply that is…

00:06:42.139 --> 00:06:45.429
unhinged. "YOU WILL SHIP.

00:06:45.429 --> 00:06:46.029
I KNOW WHERE YOU LIVE."

00:06:46.029 --> 00:06:51.259
I laugh, but it comes out like fear wearing a comedy

00:06:51.259 --> 00:06:54.879
mask. Because—no, you don't.

00:06:54.879 --> 00:06:57.969
But also—WHY ARE YOU YELLING?

00:06:59.049 --> 00:07:00.229
I take a screenshot.

00:07:00.669 --> 00:07:03.339
Then another. Then I cancel the order through the

00:07:03.349 --> 00:07:05.579
processor as a suspected fraud attempt.

00:07:06.619 --> 00:07:09.129
The dashboard updates: cancelled.

00:07:09.489 --> 00:07:11.619
Funds reversed. No shipment.

00:07:12.699 --> 00:07:14.009
I should feel relieved.

00:07:14.009 --> 00:07:16.199
But instead, I feel…

00:07:16.199 --> 00:07:21.279
shaky. Like I just stepped off a moving train.

00:07:21.279 --> 00:07:23.949
And that's when I notice something else.

00:07:24.779 --> 00:07:26.449
My site traffic spikes.

00:07:26.449 --> 00:07:27.429
Like, a lot.

00:07:28.249 --> 00:07:30.719
I open analytics.

00:07:30.719 --> 00:07:32.469
Hundreds of visitors…

00:07:32.469 --> 00:07:34.349
all hitting my checkout page.

00:07:34.349 --> 00:07:35.509
Over and over.

00:07:37.449 --> 00:07:38.619
My throat tightens.

00:07:39.669 --> 00:07:41.149
They're testing my store.

00:07:41.869 --> 00:07:43.179
Trying different cards.

00:07:43.179 --> 00:07:46.329
Different names. Seeing what sticks.

00:07:46.329 --> 00:07:52.619
I whisper to myself: "Oh my god, I'm a vending machine

00:07:52.629 --> 00:07:56.319
to them." I do the fastest "entrepreneur bootcamp"

00:07:56.319 --> 00:08:00.069
of my life in the next twenty minutes: I turn on

00:08:00.069 --> 00:08:01.179
stricter fraud filters.

00:08:01.179 --> 00:08:01.659
I block certain regions.

00:08:02.119 --> 00:08:04.609
I add address verification.

00:08:05.129 --> 00:08:07.409
I disable bulk quantities temporarily.

00:08:07.869 --> 00:08:08.839
I add a captcha.

00:08:09.869 --> 00:08:14.219
I breathe. Then, finally, the traffic drops.

00:08:14.219 --> 00:08:19.549
Silence returns. I sit there, hands on the keyboard,

00:08:19.919 --> 00:08:22.919
and I start laughing—real laughing.

00:08:23.739 --> 00:08:24.989
Not because it's funny…

00:08:24.989 --> 00:08:26.549
but because I genuinely thought entrepreneurship

00:08:26.559 --> 00:08:30.409
was going to be, like, choosing brand colors and

00:08:30.419 --> 00:08:32.649
posting motivational quotes.

00:08:33.649 --> 00:08:37.299
Turns out it's also occasionally wrestling a cyber-goblin

00:08:37.309 --> 00:08:38.239
at 2 a.m.

00:08:38.239 --> 00:08:39.259
in pajama pants.

00:08:40.589 --> 00:08:43.489
The next morning, I wake up to one new email.

00:08:44.049 --> 00:08:47.329
Subject line: "Order Inquiry (Legit)"

00:08:48.339 --> 00:08:49.659
I open it cautiously.

00:08:49.659 --> 00:08:52.809
"Hi! I run a coworking space.

00:08:52.809 --> 00:08:55.449
We want 200 planners with our logo.

00:08:55.989 --> 00:08:57.341
Can we talk?"

00:08:57.341 --> 00:08:59.145
I stare at it.

00:08:59.145 --> 00:09:00.219
My eye twitches.

00:09:01.329 --> 00:09:05.219
"Sure. Totally. Let me just recover from last night's

00:09:05.229 --> 00:09:08.419
villain arc." We hop on a call.

00:09:08.639 --> 00:09:09.509
They're real. They're friendly.

00:09:11.109 --> 00:09:12.369
They laugh at my jokes.

00:09:13.189 --> 00:09:16.409
They have a website and a phone number and—get this—a

00:09:16.419 --> 00:09:18.349
normal address with a front door.

00:09:18.349 --> 00:09:18.829
I fulfill the order.

00:09:19.909 --> 00:09:20.659
It goes smoothly.

00:09:22.719 --> 00:09:24.339
They reorder the next month.

00:09:24.339 --> 00:09:28.069
And here's the twist: That scam attempt?

00:09:28.069 --> 00:09:30.379
It didn't just scare me.

00:09:30.379 --> 00:09:32.079
It upgraded me.

00:09:32.939 --> 00:09:36.569
Because I realized something important: if my tiny

00:09:36.579 --> 00:09:39.149
little planner shop could attract fraudsters, it

00:09:39.149 --> 00:09:42.309
meant I'd built something real enough to be targeted.

00:09:43.399 --> 00:09:45.649
So I changed how I ran my business.

00:09:45.649 --> 00:09:48.079
I built simple security rules.

00:09:48.079 --> 00:09:50.429
I wrote policies in plain English.

00:09:50.429 --> 00:09:52.119
I stopped worshipping "big numbers"

00:09:52.129 --> 00:09:55.379
and started verifying reality.

00:09:56.239 --> 00:09:57.449
And the funniest part?

00:09:58.189 --> 00:10:01.039
A few months later, a friend asked, "How did you

00:10:01.049 --> 00:10:02.539
learn fraud prevention so fast?"

00:10:02.539 --> 00:10:06.009
I said, "By almost donating twelve thousand dollars

00:10:06.019 --> 00:10:09.699
worth of planners to a raccoon warehouse."

00:10:09.699 --> 00:10:13.969
Look—if you're building something, the wins feel

00:10:13.979 --> 00:10:16.529
amazing. But the near-misses?

00:10:16.529 --> 00:10:20.019
Those are the moments you actually become the person

00:10:20.029 --> 00:10:21.529
who can handle the wins.

00:10:22.579 --> 00:10:26.119
And if you ever get a massive order at 2:07 a.m.

00:10:26.119 --> 00:10:27.699
to an abandoned warehouse…

00:10:29.049 --> 00:10:29.939
Don't ship it.

00:10:29.939 --> 00:10:32.259
Ship your spine first.
